    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (73.42) serving as our premier offensive anchor. His elite score is driven by the prime leadoff spot against a manageable arm in Dotel, compounded by a strong dynamic platoon advantage that boosts his stolen base potential\u2014a critical factor given the scarcity of speed in our current build. **Josh Smith** (64.66) also projects as a high-floor play, benefiting significantly from a 14% boost due to dynamic platoon splits against Bassitt, allowing him to outperform several higher-order hitters despite batting seventh. Meanwhile, **Caleb Durbin** (63.67) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (62.05) provide reliable stability in the middle of our order, both capitalizing on favorable matchups against Lugo and Bassitt, respectively. \n\nWe face a stiff challenge in navigating high-tier arms, specifically when dealing with the elite stuff of Sale and Ullola. **Trea Turner** (52.66) remains a difficult start against Sale\u2019s 2.81 xERA, though his #2 batting position keeps his floor viable. Similarly, **Junior Caminero** (51.25) draws the toughest individual assignment of the day against Ullola; while his base talent warrants consideration, the SP skill penalty pushes him right to the edge of our starting threshold. **Carson Benge** (48.31) narrowly holds his spot, though we must keep a close watch on his performance against the tough Rod\u00f3n. \n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Chase Meidroth** (54.14), who remains the odd man out despite a solid projection. While his #1 spot in the order provided a 10% lift, his overall efficiency metrics were outclassed by the specific platoon and SB-targeting advantages held by **Josh Smith** and **Hector Rodriguez**. Furthermore, we have officially benched **Dillon Dingler** (39.24) as his projected efficiency fell below our 40-point floor due to an unfavorable platoon split, prioritizing game cap preservation over a marginal start. With **Yordan Alvarez** sidelined today, we are relying on our depth to squeeze value out of these high-speed, high-platoon matchups.",
